{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 10: a shipment pipeline. Orders leave a factory and arrive at a shop later.
  The same orders are delayed three ways: smooth, bunched (order 3) and an exact pipeline. }
Orders=
	100 + STEP(60, 10)
	~	cases/week
	~	Orders the factory ships each week. A step up at week 10.
	|
Smooth arrival=
	DELAY(Orders, 6)
	~	cases/week
	~	Material in transit for about 6 weeks, spread out.
	|
Bunched arrival=
	DELAY(Orders, 6, order=3)
	~	cases/week
	~	The same, but most of it arrives close to week 6.
	|
Pipeline arrival=
	DELAY(Orders, 6, exact=True)
	~	cases/week
	~	A pipeline: everything arrives exactly 6 weeks after it left.
	|
Belief about orders=
	DELAY(Orders, 6, kind=information)
	~	cases/week
	~	What a manager believes the orders are: a perception that catches up with the fact. Nothing is conserved.
	|
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
FINAL TIME = 40 ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = 0.25 ~ week ~ |
